  "script": [
    "This shot melts fat cells for good. It basically works like dish soap.",
    "Aqualyx is deoxycholate, a bile acid your gut uses to break up fat. In fat, it rips cells open.",
    "In a dish, it kills every cell type tested. In your body, skin and muscle proteins soak it up. Fat has few, so fat bursts.",
    "Kybella, the FDA-approved version, shrank double chins in about two thirds of people in two big trials. Placebo? About one in five.",
    "The catch: days of swelling, and four percent got a temporary nerve injury. Lopsided smile.",
    "One patient got a shot sold as Aqualyx from someone untrained: skin necrosis and painful nodules that burst open.",
    "My take: in a clinic, on a small fat pocket, it works. From a TikTok slideshow and an insulin syringe? Hard pass."
  ],
